        ":question/worked-solution": "Recall that the ellipse $\\frac{x^{2}}{25}+\\frac{y^{2}}{100}=1$ in the $xy$-plane has the parametrization\n\n$$\n\u27e8x,y\u27e9=\u27e85 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,10 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\u27e9,\\quad t\\in[0,2\\pi),\n$$\n\nsince\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x^2}{25}+\\frac{y^2}{100}&=\\frac{(5 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})^2}{25}+\\frac{(10 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})^2}{100}\\\\&=\\cos^2 t+\\sin^2 t\\\\&=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\nf(t,z)=\u27e8x,y,z\u27e9=\u27e85 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,10 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\,z\u27e9\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in[0,2\\pi)$ and $z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)$.\n\nTherefore, the second component of $f$ is $10 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}$.",
