      "question": {
        ":question/id": "d1d3e827-a6a2-556e-9878-872eebef39c3",
        ":question/problem": "$$\nf(t,y)=\u27e84 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,y,\\,\\text{_____}\u27e9\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(t,y)$ above parametrizes the elliptic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as $\\frac{x^{2}}{16}+\\frac{z^{2}}{64}=1.$ What is the third component of $f?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Recall that the ellipse $\\frac{x^{2}}{16}+\\frac{z^{2}}{64}=1$ in the $xz$-plane has the parametrization\n\n$$\n\u27e8x,z\u27e9=\u27e84 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,8 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\u27e9,\\quad t\\in[0,2\\pi),\n$$\n\nsince\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x^2}{16}+\\frac{z^2}{64}&=\\frac{(4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})^2}{16}+\\frac{(8 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})^2}{64}\\\\&=\\cos^2 t+\\sin^2 t\\\\&=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\nf(t,y)=\u27e8x,y,z\u27e9=\u27e84 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,y,\\,8 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\u27e9\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in[0,2\\pi)$ and $y\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)$.\n\nTherefore, the third component of $f$ is $8 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}$.",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
